      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That white substance is \"bloom,\" caused by fat (fat bloom) or sugar (sugar bloom) migrating to the surface, but the dull film you describe is most likely fat bloom from improper tempering. To fix it, let the chocolate rest in a cool, stable temperature for several days to allow the bloom to subside, then re-temper the chocolate by carefully melting it to exact temperatures and working it quickly to stabilize the crystal structure. Proper tempering ensures a hard snap and prevents these streaks from reappearing in the future.",
